From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show drawings in the viewport as they print

Checking how annotations, styles, symbols, hatches and text sizes come
out required opening the generated SVG outside of Bonsai after every
change. The new Print Preview toggle in the Active Drawing panel
renders the generated drawing SVG to an image and shows it in front of
the drawing camera view, matching the camera frame, with an adjustable
opacity. The preview is refreshed whenever the drawing is created and
restored when a drawing is activated.

Rendering uses the new "SVG to PNG Command" preference, falling back
to Inkscape or rsvg-convert when found.

Closes #6422.

